  "sketchNote": "A layout, not a design. The yellow blocks are your ledger spines, placed by the game three per shelf, bottom left of each bay: never draw them. The three bays behind them (the flat dark panels, 26 wide by 15 tall) are the only pixels that belong to the game: keep each one a plain back panel, fully opaque, at most 3 colours. Everything else is yours. Want a fatter frame or a taller crown? Shrink or move the bays in the slot file and keep each one at least 22 wide by 14 tall; the validator checks both."
